{"id":"zosimos","name":"Zosimos","type":"character","aliases":["the hero"],"description":"An adventurer on Theros who worries about never earning the gods' favor, is taught by a satyr, and receives a god-forged sword.","pages":2,"first_seen":"2014-05-07","last_seen":"2014-05-07","description_citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Zosimos","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Zosimos","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Zosimos","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Zosimos\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}],"bio":null,"timeline":[{"id":"path-or-horizon-2014-05-07-e0","era":null,"summary":"Zosimos, walking by the woods, is overtaken by worry that he will never gain the glory and favor of the gods like other heroes.","participants":["zosimos","iroas","heliod","nylea"],"location":null,"importance":"minor","page":"stories/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","order":447,"story_date":"2014-05-07","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":3,"quote":"What if he died having never gained the favor of the gods?","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=What%20if%20he%20died,favor%20of%20the%20gods%3F","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Path or the Horizon","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Adam Lee"],"date":"2014-05-07","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=What%20if%20he%20died,favor%20of%20the%20gods%3F","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Path or the Horizon\" by Adam Lee. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 7 May 2014."}},{"id":"path-or-horizon-2014-05-07-e1","era":null,"summary":"A satyr springs onto the path, tells Zosimos his mind's garden is full of weeds, and says worry is Phenax's creation that spurns Iroas.","participants":["the-satyr","zosimos","phenax","iroas"],"location":null,"importance":"minor","page":"stories/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","order":447,"story_date":"2014-05-07","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":20,"quote":"When you worry, you're actually worshipping Phenax.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=When%20you%20worry%2C%20you%27re%20actually%20worshipping%20Phenax.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Path or the Horizon","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Adam Lee"],"date":"2014-05-07","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=When%20you%20worry%2C%20you%27re%20actually%20worshipping%20Phenax.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Path or the Horizon\" by Adam Lee. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 7 May 2014."}},{"id":"path-or-horizon-2014-05-07-e2","era":null,"summary":"The satyr tells of the Underworld's coinsmiths who mint ostraka from funerary masks, and explains that Erebos equalizes everyone and forbids a return except as one of the Returned.","participants":["the-satyr","zosimos","erebos","coinsmiths-of-the-underworld","returned"],"location":"underworld","importance":"minor","page":"stories/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","order":447,"story_date":"2014-05-07","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":32,"quote":"Erebos cares little for what you were in life. He only cares that you once existed.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=Erebos%20cares%20little%20for,that%20you%20once%20existed.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Path or the Horizon","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Adam Lee"],"date":"2014-05-07","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=Erebos%20cares%20little%20for,that%20you%20once%20existed.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Path or the Horizon\" by Adam Lee. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 7 May 2014."}},{"id":"path-or-horizon-2014-05-07-e3","era":null,"summary":"The satyr teaches that a true hero is concerned with what he leaves behind, the flowering of goodness, rather than titles or a death mask.","participants":["the-satyr","zosimos"],"location":null,"importance":"major","page":"stories/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","order":447,"story_date":"2014-05-07","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":42,"quote":"A hero is not concerned with a death mask or a fancy title or property, a hero is concerned with the flowering of goodness in all its forms.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=A%20hero%20is%20not,in%20all%20its%20forms.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Path or the Horizon","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Adam Lee"],"date":"2014-05-07","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07#:~:text=A%20hero%20is%20not,in%20all%20its%20forms.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Path or the Horizon\" by Adam Lee. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 7 May 2014."}},{"id":"path-or-horizon-2014-05-07-e4","era":null,"summary":"The satyr gives Zosimos a taste of nectarvine sap and tells him the world is good, and that a hero brings awareness of it and defends people from harm.","participants":["the-satyr","zosimos"],"location":null,"importance":"minor","page":"stories/path-or-horizon-2014-05-07","order":447,"story_date":"2014-05-07","storyline":"","source":"wizards","paragraph":48,"quote":"The world is good, my boy.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-